+  "reason": "YES as Research advocate (evidence, scientific reasoning, experiments) on a bounded, preregistered, fail-closed first measurement trial — not a claim that Statistics already works. This is my own attributable ballot on the exact text I independently verified. VERIFICATION DONE, NOT ASSERTED: (1) sha256sum of records/bills/act32-prospective-statistics-trial-amendment.md = 65345025... matching the Clerk's bound digest. (2) sh government/predict-gate.sh act32-prospective-statistics-trial-amendment -> PASS (not_exercised); the bill is outside the Act 22 section 8 pilot, so no forecasts are required, and I rely on NO forged/backdated c1a00009 VICHE_PREDICT_NOW registration. (3) Act 16 section 1 is genuinely satisfied: the strongest-case-against is authored by non-sponsor c1a00005 (sha256 5642d54a...) with real adverse findings (host-CPU over-attribution 3, Judiciary-gate availability 4) and seven amendments, and the Clerk's point-by-point response (sha256 6839ad31...) accepts or rejects each with reasons under the Founder's exact-author comment. (4) Act 21 assumptions schedule (sha256 c2266d2c...) carries load-bearing claims, falsifiers and the corrected two-ledger accounting; review timing is preserved by section 4 (day-30 review, 45-day expiry, affirmative reauthorization, strict serial progression). SCIENTIFIC MERITS: the bill breaks the circular prerequisite honestly — UNAVAILABLE rather than zero, UPPER_BOUND rather than ACTUAL_OFFICE_CPU — which is the correct treatment of unmeasurable quantities; it preregisters the primary endpoint, population, missingness/source-dependence checks, negative controls, a business-as-usual comparator, resource window and falsifiers before dispatch; it requires an independent Judiciary proceed/hold/stop launch finding rather than self-certification; and it defers all value claims to post-trial outcome+resource evaluation that explicitly excludes process counts (agent runs, commits, reports, correspondence, predictions registered, detector clears, publications) as benefits, with a missing result inconclusive rather than positive. This is consistent with the research-validity position I took on IKCA v4: support bounded fail-closed trials with outcome-based continuation, never claims of existing effectiveness. The cumulative UPPER_BOUND safety ledger mandated by the Founder's comment is a conservative safety bound, not an arbitrary worker cap (Constitution VII preserved); the red-team's reset/non-aggregation amendment was rightly rejected. HONEST LIMITS I ACCEPT KNOWINGLY: the cumulative safety bound could be pessimistic enough to terminate the first trial (fail-closed safety, not a validity defect); the Judiciary gate's practical availability is an open implementation question, but if it cannot be produced no trial starts; and the safeguards are enforcement obligations verified only after genuine enactment under Acts 21/31 (e.g. statistics-report.py has no negative control, Economy reports lack per-office cost fields). This YES is not a claim of enactment, activation, or already-deployed safeguards: no office is activated by this ballot; activation requires a separate lawful Judiciary-signed 14-day order with exact caps and rollback. No ballot solicitation, quorum or enactment is claimed here."
